#189 two-stage accept (RULES-confirm.md, committed 29e7398e) for the #183 search driver -- w167, 11-14 CST.
Against HEAD 5f4225e7 (driver.py = 4e089db2's: strata + pool K=3 + cross). Touches search/v3/driver.py and search/v3/slices.py.
CONF "confirm" absent = today's driver event for event (test_confirm189: identity on the #183 replay and on the live K=3 state).

Choices the rule leaves open (each pinned by a test in search/v3/confirm189/test_confirm189.py):
 1 State. Stage 1 accept / join of a listed size -> "tentative" event (the stage-1 numbers, the target "inc" | "worst",
   the stage-1 reference "vs", the pool join info). It counts as the search slice's decision at once (reg.decided,
   dec, kind total), as a decision does today. Confirm evals -> "submit" (kind "confirm", "of" = the model's tag,
   "for" = the tentative or "golive") + "confirm_submit". Verdict -> "confirm" (both stages' numbers, ref, evals,
   ref_changed) then "decision" with "stage": 2, then the usual pool / incumbent events. Replay rebuilds the pending
   tentatives (tentative minus confirm), the eval cache (from the submits) and the go-live progress.
 2 Confirm evals: whole slice, no early-stop block, the slice's registry alias (hosts unchanged). Cache key (assignment
   hash, slice), so a rotation's "inc" retag is the same model. A failed eval is resubmitted; CONF tries (2) failures
   -> reject "confirm (eval failed)" (go-live: the size is kept and logged "error").
 3 Stage 2 = driver.paired(ref eval, cand eval) on the confirmation slice: per-(part, stratum) sums, stratum weights,
   CONF cap / guard as in force (both null live), offset = the candidate's recorded b x (bpw_cand - bpw_ref) + decode
   term (as on_result). z = Paired.z() = da / se (the delta-method SE behind every "z" in the log). Confirmed iff
   z < CONF z (-1.0). P.final() is recorded, not used.
 4 Reference = the size's current incumbent at the end of the confirmation (rule 3). For a join that would only
   replace the worst member: the CURRENT worst member (= "that member" unless the pool changed; if the worst is now
   the incumbent, the candidate is treated as an incumbent candidate). K > 1 waits until the pool is scored on the
   active slice (rotation rescore), since the worst is defined there.
 5 Apply against the current state: incumbent candidate -> joins (add, or replaces the current worst) and becomes
   incumbent; worst candidate -> joins without becoming incumbent, decision "join" (not "accept"), so convplot4 does
   not chain it. Kind shares count an accept only when confirmed.
 6 Plot: stage-2 decision "logr" = stage 2's P.d(), "logr1" / "z1" = stage 1's; tentatives are not decision events.
   convplot4.walk unchanged (test plot_chains_stage2_logr).
 7 Go-live: one-shot in the first step after start when CONF golive_from_line is set and no "golive" event exists:
   switch-time incumbent = the last "incumbent" event at or before that line; sizes whose current model is the same
   are "same" (no eval); others: current vs switch-time on the first pair's confirmation slice, same test; not
   confirmed -> set_incumbent(switch-time tag), pool = [it] ("pool" why "golive"). A size's tentatives wait until its
   check is resolved. b = the size's b at the start (recorded in the plan).
 8 Registry: confirmation slices carry "role": "confirm" (slices.py role REG NAME confirm). Registry.ready() /
   activate_next() / the driver's rotate() skip them; draw_merged treats their calib docs as busy; stage-2 decisions go
   to the slice's "confirm_decisions" and doc_decisions, never "decisions" (rotate_after). The driver refuses to start
   with CONF confirm unless every pair's confirmation slice has the role and was never active / decided.
 9 A tentative from a search slice with no pair waits (WARN logged once) until CONF gets a pair.
Not handled: a reselect at rotation promoting another member while a go-live check is pending is not blocked (the
check compares the planned models; a revert replaces whatever is incumbent).

